There is no .github directory in the repository, so nothing runs the test suite on a push and nothing checks the build.

The Author bundle ships a shared composite action for exactly this case, so a Getty distribution needs no test plumbing of its own:

    - uses: Getty/p5-dist-zilla-pluginbundle-author-getty/.github/actions/dzil-test@v1

Work:
- add .github/workflows/ci.yml as a pure-Perl distribution workflow: trigger on push to all branches, on tags, and on pull_request; a matrix of perl versions in the perl image containers; actions/checkout@v4; then the shared dzil-test action
- the action installs the dzil plugins through dzil authordeps and the requirements through dzil listdeps; the cpanfile has to list them for that to work
- the live test needs a network and is skipped by default - the workflow must not set the live switch, the dual stack host it uses is not reachable from every runner
- the workflow file must not end up in the built distribution; check the tarball after dzil build

Commit b23779a on offen-2610. Verified: built dist has no .github (gather_exclude_match). dzil authordeps lists the bundle and Software::License::Perl_5, so no cpanfile change was needed; live switch not set. Workflow itself not run (no push allowed).
